HeaderInclude
config/brew/brew-opts.h

msoft-float
Target Mask(SOFT_FLOAT)
Generate code with floating point emulation.

menvironment=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(brew_environment) Var(brew_environment) Init(0)
-menvironment=[user|operating]	Link for the given run-time environment: user (TASK mode, syscalls provided by the simulator or an OS; the default) or operating (bare metal, started from reset in SCHEDULER mode).

Enum
Name(brew_environment) Type(int)
Known run-time environments (for use with the -menvironment= option):

EnumValue
Enum(brew_environment) String(user) Value(0)

EnumValue
Enum(brew_environment) String(operating) Value(1)

mno-crt0
Target RejectNegative
Do not link the run-time environment's startup file (crt0.o).

mtune=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(brew_processor) Var(brew_tune_option) Init(PROCESSOR_GENERIC)
-mtune=PROCESSOR	Tune the generated code for PROCESSOR: generic (the default) or espresso.

Enum
Name(brew_processor) Type(enum brew_processor)
Known Brew processors (for use with the -mtune= option):

EnumValue
Enum(brew_processor) String(generic) Value(PROCESSOR_GENERIC)

EnumValue
Enum(brew_processor) String(espresso) Value(PROCESSOR_ESPRESSO)

march=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(brew_arch) Var(brew_arch_option) Init(BREW_ARCH_FULL)
-march=ARCH	Generate code for a core with the optional instructions ARCH names: brew (multiply and shifts; the default), brew-nomul (no multiplier), brew-noshift (no barrel shifter) or brew-min (neither).

Enum
Name(brew_arch) Type(enum brew_arch)
Known Brew architectures (for use with the -march= option):

EnumValue
Enum(brew_arch) String(brew) Value(BREW_ARCH_FULL)

EnumValue
Enum(brew_arch) String(brew-nomul) Value(BREW_ARCH_NOMUL)

EnumValue
Enum(brew_arch) String(brew-noshift) Value(BREW_ARCH_NOSHIFT)

EnumValue
Enum(brew_arch) String(brew-min) Value(BREW_ARCH_MIN)

mmul
Target Var(brew_mul) Init(1)
Use the multiply instructions (the default unless -march= names a core without a multiplier).

mshift
Target Var(brew_shift) Init(1)
Use the shift instructions (the default unless -march= names a core without a barrel shifter).
